# EVA Public Page Standard

Mirror AVR Energies marketing patterns. No admin panel in this phase.

## Architecture

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| Route `page.tsx` (or `layout.tsx`) | `metadata`, JSON-LD, server HTML |
| `src/data/*.ts` | Copy + `*_PAGE_URL` / `*_OG_IMAGE` / `*_SEO` |
| `src/components/*` | Client islands only (menu, hero, forms, modals) |

## Visual rule

Do not redesign. Preserve existing EVA CSS classes, colors and copy from `public/css`.

## SEO

- Unique title + description per route
- Canonical, robots, Open Graph, Twitter
- JSON-LD where relevant (LocalBusiness, AboutPage, ContactPage, Service)
- Keep `public/robots.txt` updated and `src/app/sitemap.ts` in sync with indexable routes

## UX / accessibility

Apply Laws of UX and WCAG 2.2 AA without changing brand look:

- Labels / `aria-invalid` / error text on forms
- Visible `:focus-visible`
- Meaningful image `alt`
- Footer on every page
- Skip link “Skip to main content” first in `(web)/layout.tsx`; every page’s `<main>` has `id="main-content" tabIndex={-1}`
- Follow `.cursor` skills `laws-of-ux-review`, `user-centered-design`, `wcag-22-aa-audit` (WCAG 2.2 AA, targets ≥ 24px, 44px for primary actions)

## Images

- First visible image on every page: `loading="eager"` + `fetchPriority="high"`. In lists, spread `imageLoading(i)` from `src/lib/image-loading.ts`.
- Every other image is lazy (`next/image` default; plain `<img>` needs `loading="lazy"`).
- Never use the deprecated `priority` prop and don't combine `preload` with `loading` / `fetchPriority`.
- Prefer `next/image` `fill` over CSS `background-image` so it can lazy-load. A CSS background that is the main image gets one `<link rel="preload" as="image" fetchPriority="high">`.
- Site images are AVIF under 150 KB: drop the JPG/PNG into `public/images/` and run `npm run images`.
- Social previews stay JPG (platforms don't read AVIF): each page has its own 1200x630 `public/images/og/<page>.jpg` with an `*_OG_IMAGE_ALT`, built by the same script.
- Decorative photo animations: `ImageEffects` + positions in `src/data/image-fx.ts`; keep them `aria-hidden` and off under reduced motion.

## Analytics

Do not add GTM (or other analytics) to individual pages. Public pages under `(web)` inherit `GtmHead` / `GtmNoscript` from `src/app/(web)/layout.tsx`.

## Checklist

1. Add route under `src/app/(web)/` (inherits GTM) plus `src/constants/routes.ts` and nav if needed
2. Add `src/data/<page>.ts` with SEO constants
3. Server page + client islands only where interactive
4. Update `src/app/sitemap.ts` (and robots.txt if needed)
5. `npm run build`
